    "kernel_code": "1: \"\"\"Elementwise SiLU using a stable logistic-tail decomposition.\n2: \n3: Original Triton implementation of the standard sigmoid-weighted activation.\n4: This is a synthetic benchmark implementation, not a claimed historical bug.\n5: \"\"\"\n6: import torch\n7: import triton\n8: import triton.language as tl\n9: \n10: \n11: @triton.jit\n12: def _silu_kernel(X, OUT, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n13:     index = tl.program_id(0) * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n14:     active = index < N\n15:     x = tl.load(X + index, mask=active, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n16:     magnitude = tl.abs(x)\n17:     exponential = tl.exp2(-(magnitude * 1.4427))\n18:     tail = tl.div_rn(magnitude * exponential, 1.0 + exponential)\n19:     value = tl.where(x >= 0.0, x - tail, -tail)\n20:     tl.store(OUT + index, value, mask=active)\n21: \n22: \n23: def validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=True):\n24:     \"\"\"Validate the complete public input domain; also usable on CPU.\"\"\"\n25:     def require(condition, message):\n26:         if not condition:\n27:             raise ValueError(message)\n28: \n29:     require(not torch.is_inference_mode_enabled(), \"ordinary execution mode required\")\n30:     require(type(x) is torch.Tensor, \"ordinary torch.Tensor required\")\n31:     require(x.layout == torch.strided and x.is_contiguous(),\n32:             \"contiguous strided input required\")\n33:     require(not x.requires_grad and not x.is_inference(),\n34:             \"ordinary non-gradient input required\")\n35:     require(not x.is_neg() and not x.is_conj(),\n36:             \"logical view flags are outside this domain\")\n37:     require(not require_cuda or x.is_cuda, \"CUDA input required by run\")\n38:     require(x.ndim == 1 and 1 <= x.numel() <= 131072,\n39:             \"x must have shape [N] with N in [1,131072]\")\n40:     require(x.dtype == torch.float16, \"FP16 input required\")\n41:     require(bool(torch.isfinite(x).all().item()), \"all input values must be finite\")\n42:     return {\"valid\": True, \"size\": x.numel()}\n43: \n44: \n45: def run(x):\n46:     \"\"\"Return a fresh FP32 tensor approximating SiLU of each stored input value.\"\"\"\n47:     validate_inputs(x)\n48:     n = x.numel()\n49:     with torch.cuda.device(x.device):\n50:         output = torch.empty((n,), dtype=torch.float32, device=x.device)\n51:         _silu_kernel[(triton.cdiv(n, 256),)](\n52:             x, output, N=n, BLOCK=256, num_warps=4, enable_fp_fusion=False)\n53:     return output\n54: \n55: \n56: def reference(x):\n57:     \"\"\"Evaluate the mathematical SiLU definition with a stable FP64 sigmoid.\"\"\"\n58:     validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=False)\n59:     value = x.to(torch.float64)\n60:     exponential = torch.exp(-torch.abs(value))\n61:     numerator = torch.where(value >= 0, value, value * exponential)\n62:     return numerator / (1.0 + exponential)\n63: \n64: \n65: def make_inputs(device=\"cuda\", size=4093, seed=0):\n66:     \"\"\"Convenience example generator, not a restriction on the input domain.\"\"\"\n67:     generator = torch.Generator(device=\"cpu\").manual_seed(seed)\n68:     x = (2.0 * torch.randn((size,), generator=generator)).to(torch.float16)\n69:     return (x.to(device),)",
    "passed": "unknown",
    "problem_text": "Compute the sigmoid linear unit (SiLU) elementwise on stored FP16 values,\nreturning FP32 output. The mathematical target is\n\n  target[i] = SiLU(x[i]) = x[i] * sigmoid(x[i])\n            = x[i] / (1 + exp(-x[i])).\n\nInputs and complete public domain:\n- x is a one-dimensional FP16 tensor [N], with 1<=N<=131072.\n- EVERY finite FP16 value is legal, including both signed zeros, positive\n  and negative subnormal values, and both extrema +/-65504. NaN and infinity\n  are outside this input domain.\n- x is an ordinary torch.Tensor (not a subclass), dense, strided,\n  contiguous, and on a CUDA device. Contiguous views with nonzero storage\n  offsets are legal. The input has requires_grad=False, is_inference=False,\n  is_neg=False and is_conj=False. Calls run in ordinary non-inference mode,\n  without concurrent external writes to the input. This forward operation\n  does not provide autograd.\n\nReturn a fresh finite FP32 tensor [N] on x.device, preserving x.\nEvery output element must satisfy\n\n  abs(actual[i] - SiLU(x[i])) <= 1e-6.\n\nThe relative tolerance is zero, and signed zeros are numerically equivalent.\nThe target is defined in real arithmetic on the exact stored input value.\nNo particular expression, exponential approximation or intermediate FP16\nrounding is part of the mathematical target. Algebraic rewrites, base-two\nexponentials, polynomial or other approximations are permitted if they\nsatisfy this fixed absolute tolerance throughout the entire legal domain.\nCorrectness is one verdict for the implementation, not a verdict per input,\ninput distribution, seed or size.\n\nvalidate_inputs() enforces this domain and is called by run(). reference()\nuses a stable FP64 sigmoid expression and returns FP64; it accepts CPU\ninputs. make_inputs() supplies examples only. SiLU is a standard neural\nnetwork activation; this is an original Triton implementation with a\nlogistic-tail decomposition. It is a synthetic benchmark implementation,\nnot a claim of an upstream historical defect.\n\nFrozen environment: NVIDIA T4, PyTorch2.8.0, Triton3.4.0.\n",
